<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Quick Start</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00005</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Quick Start</md:title>
    <md:uuid>bbd428d3-79a9-4011-9e1c-966f1251605c</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <para>Welcome to your Algebra 1 module! We're genuinely excited for you to join our community
        and embark on a transformative learning journey!</para>
      <para>This user-friendly guide is your roadmap to navigating the features and resources of our
        unique Algebra I content. Let's raise the bar on your algebra skills—get started with
        confidence today!</para>
      <section>
        <title>I. Where to Start</title>
        <table>
          <tgroup cols="2">
            <tbody>
              <row>
                <entry>
                  <figure>
                    <media alt="Scatter Plot">
                      <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_00_02_01_01.png" />
                    </media>
                    <caption>Image 1</caption>
                  </figure>
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  <figure>
                    <media alt="Line of Best Fit">
                      <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_00_02_01_02.png" />
                    </media>
                    <caption>Image 2</caption>
                  </figure>
                </entry>
              </row>
            </tbody>
          </tgroup>
        </table>

        <section>
          <title>View Lessons in the Course:</title>
          <list list-type="enumerated">
            <item>Go to “My courses” then click your Algebra course tile (Image 1)</item>
            <item>View lessons by clicking on the unit you would like to see. You can view the
              lessons in every unit by clicking “Expand all” (Image 2)</item>
          </list>
        </section>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title>II. Unit Structure</title>
        <table>
          <tgroup cols="2">
            <tbody>
              <row>
                <entry>
                  <figure>
                    <media alt="BU">
                      <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_00_02_01_03.png" />
                    </media>
                    <caption>Image 3</caption>
                  </figure>
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  <figure>
                    <media alt="EU">
                      <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_00_02_01_04.png" />
                    </media>
                    <caption>Image 4</caption>
                  </figure>
                </entry>
              </row>
            </tbody>
          </tgroup>
        </table>
        <para><emphasis>Overview and Readiness:</emphasis> Before starting a new unit we recommend
          taking the overview and readiness lesson. This will help you review topics for the unit
          and prepare for the new material you will be learning (Image 3).</para>
        <para><emphasis>Sections:</emphasis> After the overview and readiness lesson, the rest of
          the lessons are organized into sections. At the end of each section you will have an
          opportunity to test out your new algebra skills with a section quiz (Image 3).</para>
        <para><emphasis>Quizzes:</emphasis> At the end of each unit you will find a Unit Quiz, and a
          STAAR Review (Image 4).</para>
        <para><emphasis>Additional Items:</emphasis> At the end of each unit you will also find a
          project and wrap up page covering the topics in the unit (Image 4).</para>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title>III. Lesson Structure</title>
        <figure>
          <media alt="Lesson Overview">
            <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_00_02_01_05.png" />
          </media>
          <caption>Image 5</caption>
        </figure>
        <section>
          <title>Lesson Activities</title>
          <para>The first page of a lesson is called “Lesson Overview.” Here you will find the
            different types of activities included in the lesson (Image 5).</para>
          <list>
            <item><emphasis>Warm up:</emphasis> This is the first activity in a lesson.</item>
            <item><emphasis>Primary activities:</emphasis> These are unique and need extra focus.
              We'll take a close look at them in the next part of this guide.</item>
            <item><emphasis>Cool-down:</emphasis> This is the last activity in a lesson.</item>
            <item><emphasis>Practice:</emphasis> This is a practice page with problems on the topics
              you learned in the lesson.</item>
          </list>
        </section>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title>IV. Primary Activities</title>
        <table>
          <tgroup cols="2">
            <tbody>
              <row>
                <entry>
                  <figure>
                    <media alt="Primary Activity">
                      <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_00_02_01_06.png" />
                    </media>
                    <caption>Image 6</caption>
                  </figure>
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  <figure>
                    <media alt="Self Check">
                      <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_00_02_01_07.png" />
                    </media>
                    <caption>Image 7</caption>
                  </figure>
                </entry>
              </row>
            </tbody>
          </tgroup>
        </table>
        <section>
          <title>Primary Activities</title>
          <para>Here's an example of one of these unique types of activities. Each lesson has 2-3 of
            these. After you have finished the activity you will take a multiple choice question
            called, “Self Check.”</para>
          <list>
            <item><emphasis>Are you ready for more?: </emphasis>This button opens additional
              questions for you to expand your thinking. This section is optional, unless otherwise
              stated by your teacher (Image 6).</item>
            <item><emphasis>Tip:</emphasis> After completing an activity, be sure to press the
              “Next” button at the bottom of the page. This will take you to the self check
              question.</item>
          </list>
          <section>
            <title>Self Check</title>
            <para>This is a self check question (Image 7). If you get the answer correct,
              congratulations you get to move on to the next activity! If you get the answer
              incorrect, you will be directed to an additional resource page where you can review
              the topics and retake the self check question.</para>
          </section>
        </section>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title>V. End of Lesson</title>
        <table>
          <tgroup cols="2">
            <tbody>
              <row>
                <entry>
                  <figure>
                    <media alt="Lesson Summary">
                      <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_00_02_01_08.png" />
                    </media>
                    <caption>Image 8</caption>
                  </figure>
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  <figure>
                    <media alt="End of Lesson">
                      <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_00_02_01_09.png" />
                    </media>
                    <caption>Image 9</caption>
                  </figure>
                </entry>
              </row>
            </tbody>
          </tgroup>
        </table>
        <section>
          <title>Lesson Summary</title>
          <para>Here you will review the topics covered and the activities you completed (Image 8).
            You will also have an opportunity to check-in on your progress with the learning goals
            from the lesson.</para>
          <list>
            <item><emphasis>Tip:</emphasis> Once you have completed the lesson be sure to press “End
              of Lesson” so your teacher knows you have completed the lesson.</item>
          </list>
        </section>
        <section>
          <title>End of Lesson</title>
          <para>After pressing the “End of Lesson” button you will be brought to this page (Image
            9). Where you can continue to the next lesson or return to the course page.</para>
        </section>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>